      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_b3a065c1f2b0b41fa41c0ac97b9055434792c1a48447e8b47370bb1afdb659e1",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The source constructs a local-global feedback loop for analytic control: local Langlands parameters define finite and archimedean factors and expose positive square certificates or pole locations; global Rankin-Selberg continuation, holomorphy, poles, and coefficient estimates then constrain those local parameters; the resulting finite-place and baseline archimedean bounds support the global explicit-formula and prime-sum analysis.",
