    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_c02590dc6bf694b1ebcb344ab28692da991da09e2dc3aa10a69876b077b0c1f3",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The source builds the GUE correlation law through a dependency chain: smoothing and the explicit formula replace zero statistics by Fourier-localized prime sums; the support bound and integer discreteness force exact multiplicative diagonals; only balanced distinct-prime pairings survive at main order under the universal coefficient second moment; partition-lattice inversion restores distinct zero indices; and the cycle expansion of the sine-kernel determinant identifies the resulting distribution with GUE.",
