      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_ee1270c16c11f69578a2293b04064ffb6e760ea90676e76d5f22fa09bb97dec3",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Fourier support acts as an analytic dominance boundary: it bounds the prime-product scale tightly enough for the proved diagonal reduction, while the source's off-diagonal heuristic predicts that for higher-degree cusp-form coefficients cancellation could keep diagonals dominant beyond the proved 2/m range, up to the degree-one boundary of total support 2.",
